1680
01:26:02.310 --> 01:26:04.850
We didn't know if it was changing their lives.

1681
01:26:04.850 --> 01:26:06.910
We knew how much carbon we were displacing

1682
01:26:06.910 --> 01:26:10.360
because prior to the solar, they were using kerosene, right,

1683
01:26:10.360 --> 01:26:15.360
which is dirty and dangerous and terrible for your health.

1684
01:26:17.470 --> 01:26:20.040
But we developed something called lean data,

1685
01:26:20.040 --> 01:26:25.040
which is a way of texting 5, 10,000 customers simultaneously

1686
01:26:25.970 --> 01:26:27.500
asking them a series of questions

1687
01:26:27.500 --> 01:26:29.460
from which we could deduce,

1688
01:26:29.460 --> 01:26:31.370
how many more hours were you staying up at night?

1689
01:26:31.370 --> 01:26:32.990
What do you do with that time?

1690
01:26:32.990 --> 01:26:36.960
Do your children do better or worse at school?

1691
01:26:36.960 --> 01:26:38.180
What do you like about this?

1692
01:26:38.180 --> 01:26:40.310
Would you recommend it to your neighbors?

1693
01:26:40.310 --> 01:26:41.910
Et cetera, et cetera, et cetera.

1694
01:26:43.485 --> 01:26:46.230
So today we're the largest off-grid

1695
01:26:46.230 --> 01:26:47.880
energy investor in the world.

1696
01:26:47.880 --> 01:26:49.730
One third of people on the planet

1697
01:26:49.730 --> 01:26:54.400
who have access to off-grid solar and light and electricity,

1698
01:26:54.400 --> 01:26:57.573
our customers of the companies in which we've invested.

1699
01:26:58.760 --> 01:27:01.740
We have a very good idea of which companies

1700
01:27:01.740 --> 01:27:04.460
are most effective at reaching the poor people,

1701
01:27:04.460 --> 01:27:05.960
reaching low income people.

1702
01:27:05.960 --> 01:27:07.200
Which companies

1703
01:27:09.830 --> 01:27:14.420
have the most effective light luminocity?

1704
01:27:14.420 --> 01:27:15.993
So the bright light.

1705
01:27:17.280 --> 01:27:20.183
Which are best for displacing carbon?

1706
01:27:22.140 --> 01:27:25.480
Which companies provide the greatest customer satisfaction?

1707
01:27:25.480 --> 01:27:28.650
And so we can now make decisions

1708
01:27:28.650 --> 01:27:30.510
for how we allocate our capital based,

1709
01:27:30.510 --> 01:27:32.860
not just on financial performance,

1710
01:27:32.860 --> 01:27:34.660
but from all these other indicators.

1711
01:27:35.770 --> 01:27:36.603
Yeah, it's beautiful.

1712
01:27:36.603 --> 01:27:38.220
I mean, those are things that are never gonna show up

1713
01:27:38.220 --> 01:27:40.480
on a spreadsheet, like how many young people

1714
01:27:40.480 --> 01:27:42.460
stayed up an extra hour to study,

1715
01:27:42.460 --> 01:27:45.310
and how do you gauge the long term impact

1716
01:27:45.310 --> 01:27:47.430
of something like that purely

1717
01:27:47.430 --> 01:27:51.610
because somebody has a light that they didn't have before.

1718
01:27:51.610 --> 01:27:54.010
And Rich, you talk about dignity.

1719
01:27:54.010 --> 01:27:58.080
If you wanna see dignity manifest,

1720
01:27:58.080 --> 01:28:03.080
go into someone's house who has forever,

1721
