And I thought, God bless you, God bless your generation.

2309
01:56:47.340 --> 01:56:50.140
That it isn't binary.

2310
01:56:50.140 --> 01:56:53.470
We can't just be nationalist or globalist.

2311
01:56:53.470 --> 01:56:54.763
We have to be both.

2312
01:56:56.117 --> 01:56:57.740
And it's not just our connection

2313
01:56:57.740 --> 01:56:59.250
and our connectedness to each other.

2314
01:56:59.250 --> 01:57:00.833
It's to all living things.

2315
01:57:02.420 --> 01:57:06.550
Teilhard de Chardin who's a Jesuit philosopher who I love

2316
01:57:06.550 --> 01:57:08.053
and read a lot of said,

2317
01:57:10.397 --> 01:57:15.397
"We are not human beings having a spiritual experience.

2318
01:57:15.690 --> 01:57:19.687
We are spiritual beings having a human experience."

2319
01:57:22.320 --> 01:57:27.040
And so I use the word moral almost as proxy

2320
01:57:27.040 --> 01:57:31.360
for that transcendent, for that spiritual, for that belief

2321
01:57:31.360 --> 01:57:36.360
that we are on this earth together for a very short moment.

2322
01:57:37.240 --> 01:57:40.120
And I believe that we come in almost as circles

2323
01:57:40.120 --> 01:57:43.653
and you and I are in a circle of a generation.

2324
01:57:44.670 --> 01:57:47.740
It goes in a second.

2325
01:57:47.740 --> 01:57:49.390
How do we use that time?

2326
01:57:49.390 --> 01:57:52.930
How do we wanna be remembered by those future generations?

2327
01:57:52.930 --> 01:57:55.780
I certainly don't want them to look back at us and think,

2328
01:57:57.540 --> 01:58:00.733
we didn't care, but that we tried.

2329
01:58:01.570 --> 01:58:05.190
And it's only when we see

2330
01:58:05.190 --> 01:58:10.190
that we are not just part of each other, we are each other,

2331
01:58:10.320 --> 01:58:12.943
that I think we'll really solve these problems.

2332
01:58:14.310 --> 01:58:16.143
That's so beautifully put,

2333
01:58:16.995 --> 01:58:18.220
and I have a million other things

2334
01:58:18.220 --> 01:58:19.480
that I'd like to talk to you about,

2335
01:58:19.480 --> 01:58:22.750
but I think you just stuck the landing

2336
01:58:22.750 --> 01:58:24.730
and I don't even wanna say anything else.

2337
01:58:24.730 --> 01:58:26.740
You could still say.

2338
01:58:26.740 --> 01:58:29.930
But I do, I guess before we round this out,

2339
01:58:29.930 --> 01:58:34.930
I do wanna leave people with a few thoughts.

2340
01:58:35.060 --> 01:58:35.893
You know, I think a lot,

2341
01:58:35.893 --> 01:58:38.860
I think most people are struggling with trying to figure out

2342
01:58:38.860 --> 01:58:41.140
how to build more purpose into their lives

2343
01:58:41.140 --> 01:58:43.750
or find a way to be more fulfilled

2344
01:58:43.750 --> 01:58:47.070
or, you know, how can I be more service-oriented

2345
01:58:47.070 --> 01:58:48.820
in the free time that I have.

2346
01:58:48.820 --> 01:58:51.860
So how do you think about helping to,

2347
01:58:51.860 --> 01:58:55.557
you know, catalyze people on this journey of trying to,

2348
01:58:55.557 --> 01:58:58.150
you know, figure that out for themselves

2349
01:58:58.150 --> 01:59:00.233
and contribute along the way?

2350
01:59:04.410 --> 01:59:07.160
Well, I have two answers to that.

2351
01:59:07.160 --> 01:59:10.310
And one, I hope doesn't sound self-promotional,

2352
01:59:10.310 --> 01:59:13.780
but the first answer is if a young person comes to me,

2353
01:59:13.780 --> 01:59:15.430
it's really asking them

2354
01:59:18.310 --> 01:59:20.220
what do they love doing?

2355
01:59:20.220 --> 01:59:21.340
What are they good at doing?

2356
01:59:21.340 --> 01:59:23.370
What does the world need from them?

2357
01:59:23.370 --> 01:59:24.890
Again, the Jesuits would say,

2358
01:59:24.890 --> 01:59:27.570
go to where your deepest journey meets the world great need.

2359
01:59:27.570 --> 01:59:30.713
And too often, we start with the I.

2360
01:59:32.350 --> 01:59:34.260
What's my purpose, what's my passion,

2361
01:59:34.260 --> 01:59:39.040
rather than if you see a problem that interests you,

2362
01:59:39.040 --> 01:59:41.590
go toward it, be curious about it.

2363
01:59:41.590 --> 01:59:45.500
I have story after story of people who just start that way

2364
01:59:45.500 --> 01:59:48.010
and end up making this their lives work.

2365
01:59:48.010 --> 01:59:51.620
If you still have no clue as to what you do next,

2366
01:59:51.620 --> 01:59:56.070
find a leader that you admire and get close to that person,

2367
01:59:56.070 --> 01:59:57.023
learn from them.

2368
01:59:59.024 --> 02:00:01.923
You never know what direction that person will bring you.

2369
02:00:02.900 --> 02:00:05.770
But because so many people were coming to us

2370
02:00:05.770 --> 02:00:07.563
and coming to me over the years,

2371
02:00:08.710 --> 02:00:11.530
we started first a fellows program at Acumen

2372
02:00:11.530 --> 02:00:13.890
where we brought people in for a year

2373
02:00:13.890 --> 02:00:16.290
and we put them in our companies around the world.

2374
02:00:16.290 --> 02:00:18.840
And then we started fellows programs

2375
02:00:18.840 --> 02:00:20.380
within country after country.

2376
02:00:20.380 --> 02:00:23.300
And now we have about a thousand fellows across the world

2377
02:00:23.300 --> 02:00:25.250
who are doing just amazing things

2378
02:00:25.250 --> 02:00:28.743
across race, class, ethnicity, religion.

2379
02:00:31.636 --> 02:00:35.380
And then we thought we should start sharing this.

2380
02:00:35.380 --> 02:00:38.120
And so we built Acumen Academy

2381
02:00:38.120 --> 02:00:39.950
as the world school for social change.

2382
02:00:39.950 --> 02:00:42.680
So it's an online, this is the self promotional part.

2383
02:00:42.680 --> 02:00:45.860
It's an online platform where anyone anywhere

2384
02:00:45.860 --> 02:00:50.860
can take a series of courses that start with, who am I?

2385
02:00:52.290 --> 02:00:53.460
What can I build?

2386
02:00:53.460 --> 02:00:58.160
Because this is a moment that needs all of us.

2387
02:00:58.160 --> 02:01:00.250
It needs us to be conscious

2388
02:01:02.040 --> 02:01:07.040
about how we spend our money, who do we give it to?

2389
02:01:07.670 --> 02:01:08.830
What do we do?

2390
02:01:08.830 --> 02:01:10.323
How do we spend our time?

2391
02:01:12.440 --> 02:01:14.560
With whom do we walk?

2392
02:01:14.560 --> 02:01:15.770
My grandmother always said,

2393
02:01:15.770 --> 02:01:19.330
show me who you walk with and I'll show you who you are.

2394
02:01:19.330 --> 02:01:24.330
And so the purpose-driven life isn't necessarily

2395
02:01:27.420 --> 02:01:29.200
under this rubric of

2396
02:01:32.420 --> 02:01:35.950
someone that's deserving of a medal or what have you.

2397
02:01:35.950 --> 02:01:38.440
It's a life that's intentional.

2398
02:01:38.440 --> 02:01:43.280
It's a life that's conscious of our action and our inaction.

2399
02:01:43.280 --> 02:01:45.173
It's a life that's full of curiosity.

2400
02:01:46.080 --> 02:01:50.790
It's a life that does a regular accounting

2401
02:01:50.790 --> 02:01:53.480
of whether you're giving more than you're taking.

2402
02:01:53.480 --> 02:01:57.363
And that asks regularly, not,

2403
02:01:58.610 --> 02:02:01.600
am I getting richer, thinner, more beautiful,

2404
02:02:01.600 --> 02:02:05.860
but what am I doing to give other people a sense of self,

2405
02:02:05.860 --> 02:02:09.510
a sense of their beauty, a sense of their possibility,

2406
02:02:09.510 --> 02:02:10.760
a sense of their dignity.

2407
02:02:14.140 --> 02:02:15.240
I think that's what it's all about.

2408
02:02:15.240 --> 02:02:17.573
Yeah, thank you for that.

2409
02:02:19.590 --> 02:02:21.840
I think that's the final word.

2410
02:02:21.840 --> 02:02:22.900
You just want me to shut up?

2411
02:02:22.900 --> 02:02:25.630
No, I don't, we've been going for two hours.

2412
02:02:25.630 --> 02:02:27.190
I could go for another two hours.

2413
02:02:27.190 --> 02:02:29.633
I wanna leave people wanting more though.

2414
02:02:31.708 --> 02:02:33.720
What a beautiful soul you are, thank you so much.

2415
02:02:33.720 --> 02:02:36.410
I really appreciate you sharing today

2416
02:02:36.410 --> 02:02:39.640
and I just feel good in your presence.

2417
02:02:39.640 --> 02:02:42.630
You know, you have a really great energy about you

2418
02:02:42.630 --> 02:02:47.630
and I have so much respect for the work that you do

2419
02:02:47.630 --> 02:02:51.870
and appreciate you sharing it today.

2420
02:02:51.870 --> 02:02:55.130
The book is "Manifesto For a Moral Revolution."

2421
02:02:55.130 --> 02:02:58.720
Have you read "The Book of Hope,"

2422
02:02:58.720 --> 02:03:01.820
the book that came out about Jane Goodall?

2423
02:03:01.820 --> 02:03:02.720
I have it, I haven't read it yet.

2424
02:03:02.720 --> 02:03:06.680
Jane Goodall is who I wanna be when I grow up.

2425
02:03:06.680 --> 02:03:10.750
There's a lot of parallels between your book and that book

2426
02:03:10.750 --> 02:03:12.363
in the sensibility, like this,

2427
02:03:13.430 --> 02:03:15.880
I felt like a sensibility that you share with Jane

2428
02:03:15.880 --> 02:03:19.980
in this like "Audacity of Hope" throughout her life

2429
02:03:19.980 --> 02:03:21.950
and all of the amazing things that she's done,

2430
02:03:21.950 --> 02:03:23.140
like holding onto hope

2431
02:03:23.140 --> 02:03:27.310
and having this optimistic but fierce disposition

2432
02:03:28.190 --> 02:03:31.980
and commitment to continuing to solve these big problems

2433
02:03:31.980 --> 02:03:36.400
and this reverence and excitement that she has

2434
02:03:36.400 --> 02:03:39.250
about the younger generations and all of-

2435
02:03:39.250 --> 02:03:44.120
There's a lot of shared like thematic sensibility

2436
02:03:44.120 --> 02:03:45.530
in your book with her book.

2437
02:03:45.530 --> 02:03:48.783
Well, that is the biggest honor you could pay me.

2438
02:03:51.570 --> 02:03:54.040
I've had the privilege of meeting her a few times

2439
02:03:54.040 --> 02:03:57.500
and talk about being in someone's presence,

2440
02:03:57.500 --> 02:04:00.633
she's a extraordinary and she's a lighthouse.

2441
02:04:01.550 --> 02:04:05.293
Where I think you also share,

2442
02:04:09.070 --> 02:04:11.640
this is a moment where so many people

2443
02:04:11.640 --> 02:04:14.380
move from places of disrespect from shaming

2444
02:04:14.380 --> 02:04:19.380
and throwing dispersions.

2445
02:04:19.590 --> 02:04:24.590
Jane focuses on the possible, on seeing goodness,

2446
02:04:25.250 --> 02:04:27.940
on building from that goodness.

2447
02:04:27.940 --> 02:04:31.670
And I've never heard her shame

2448
02:04:34.120 --> 02:04:36.120
in ways that demean.

2449
02:04:36.120 --> 02:04:41.120
She alights, ever, ever, and we need more of that.

2450
02:04:42.190 --> 02:04:43.800
And it can be complicated

2451
02:04:43.800 --> 02:04:47.820
because sometimes it seems to a younger person,

2452
02:04:47.820 --> 02:04:49.283
or maybe just any people,

2453
02:04:50.120 --> 02:04:51.683
sometimes it seems that,

2454
02:04:53.260 --> 02:04:55.270
well, you're not truth telling,

2455
02:04:55.270 --> 02:04:58.770
you're not really standing on what's right,

2456
02:04:58.770 --> 02:05:00.880
rather than, oh yes, you are.

2457
02:05:00.880 --> 02:05:04.133
And you try to cross her, you won't get very far.

2458
02:05:05.860 --> 02:05:07.060
And I feel the same.

2459
02:05:07.060 --> 02:05:10.600
But really understanding the psychology of change, right?

2460
02:05:10.600 --> 02:05:12.410
Shaming people isn't gonna move the needle.

2461
02:05:12.410 --> 02:05:14.510
It might make you momentarily feel

2462
02:05:15.490 --> 02:05:18.390
bigger than the other person, but that's a fleeting thing.

2463
02:05:19.429 --> 02:05:21.440
I've never seen it push people to act.

2464
02:05:21.440 --> 02:05:23.670
No, of course not, right.

2465
02:05:23.670 --> 02:05:25.240
So you have to consensus build,

2466
02:05:25.240 --> 02:05:28.370
you have to work within systems and outside of systems.

2467
02:05:28.370 --> 02:05:30.990
And we need all manner of revolutionaries.

2468
02:05:30.990 --> 02:05:33.720
We need the people on the edges as well

2469
02:05:33.720 --> 02:05:35.250
holding everyone else accountable.

2470
02:05:35.250 --> 02:05:37.160
Like all voices are needed.

2471
02:05:37.160 --> 02:05:40.560
But I think you sit in this place

2472
02:05:40.560 --> 02:05:43.030
where you have this facility for creating,

2473
02:05:43.030 --> 02:05:48.030
like taking the mechanisms of banking

2474
02:05:48.530 --> 02:05:50.210
and all these things that most people

2475
02:05:50.210 --> 02:05:53.090
don't understand at all and getting them to work

2476
02:05:53.090 --> 02:05:56.950
in unison with a purpose and a goal

2477
02:05:56.950 --> 02:05:58.700
that I think we can all get behind.

2478
02:05:59.750 --> 02:06:01.080
Well, let's be really clear,

2479
02:06:01.080 --> 02:06:02.990
I hire people who are a lot smarter than me.

2480
02:06:02.990 --> 02:06:05.753
Well, that's smart too, yeah.

2481
02:06:07.600 --> 02:06:10.160
But yeah, I do think that that is what it's about.

2482
02:06:10.160 --> 02:06:13.480
We've got the tools, we've got the skills.

2483
02:06:13.480 --> 02:06:16.060
We certainly have capital as a world.

2484
02:06:16.060 --> 02:06:18.370
And that is where that piece of moral imagination,

2485
02:06:18.370 --> 02:06:22.830
that consciousness that we are in this together

2486
02:06:22.830 --> 02:06:25.300
and that we rise and we fall together

2487
02:06:25.300 --> 02:06:28.490
is the piece that we've got to hold together,

2488
02:06:28.490 --> 02:06:31.080
whether we're the storytellers and the amplifiers

2489
02:06:31.080 --> 02:06:33.230
or the builders, whether we're the entrepreneurs

2490
02:06:33.230 --> 02:06:36.783
or the financiers, we're all needed.

2491
02:06:38.330 --> 02:06:39.867
Amen, sister.
Amen.

2492
02:06:39.867 --> 02:06:44.140
All right, "Manifesto For a Moral Revolution,"

2493
02:06:44.140 --> 02:06:46.500
pick it up wherever you buy books.

2494
02:06:46.500 --> 02:06:49.810
And Jacqueline, you're easy to find on the internet.

2495
02:06:49.810 --> 02:06:51.850
Where's the place you want to direct people?

2496
02:06:51.850 --> 02:06:54.010
To acumen?
Yeah, acumen.org,

2497
02:06:54.010 --> 02:06:55.230
on the website.

2498
02:06:55.230 --> 02:06:57.763
All right, and come back and talk to me again sometime.

2499
02:06:57.763 --> 02:06:59.120
I would love it.
Delightful.

2500
02:06:59.120 --> 02:07:00.450
I really appreciate it.

2501
02:07:00.450 --> 02:07:01.283
Thank you.

2502
02:07:01.283 --> 02:07:02.172
Thanks.
Thank you.

2503
02:07:02.172 --> 02:07:03.005
Peace.

2504
02:07:04.743 --> 02:07:07.326
(upbeat music)

